</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Traffic model:</span>
We define the request rate as the exogenous arrivals per second (req/s).
In our experiments, we generate arrivals with a Poisson process.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SLOs:</span>
Following the convention of prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agrawal et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kamath et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al. (2025)</a></cite>, the TBT SLO is set to <math id="S5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\sim}5\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∼</mo><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}5\times</annotation></semantics></math> the time to process 32 decode batches at 4096 tokens. The TTFT SLO is chosen separately for each model-dataset pair to reflect an appropriate operating point. All SLO settings are summarized in Table <a href="#S5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 5.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 5 Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. SLO attainment is evaluated per request: a request attains the SLO if its TTFT meets the TTFT SLO and, thereafter, the TBT of all generated tokens meets the TBT SLO.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Energy:</span>
We measured the total energy consumed by the GPU devices during LLM serving using NVML’s API <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">NVIDIA (2025)</a></cite>. Because NVML’s API returns the cumulative energy used from the time the driver was loaded to the time of the call, we obtain a task’s energy by invoking it at the start and end of the task and taking the difference. Energy per token was measured as the total energy divided by the total number of prompt and generated tokens.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>SLO constraints for the ShareGPT and arXiv datasets.</figcaption>
